00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.830
He ignored me.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.740
Kuroba.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:58.660
Huh?

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:02.910
Apparently Haijima played
volleyball at his last school

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.950
and will be joining the team here.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.830
Make sure you show him the ropes.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:11.990
Haijima, you can take
the seat in front of Kuroba.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.100
What position?

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.740
Huh?

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.240
What position do you play?
You're on the volleyball team, right?

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:26.540
Oh, that's what you meant.
Honestly, I don't think I have a set position.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:30.240
You don't have one? Then what
do you do during matches?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.410
I've never played in an actual match,
and our practices are whenever.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.410
It's a team filled with guys who needed
to put something down as a club.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:43.660
You know, we have to be in some
kind of club or team at our school, so...

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.740
I guess you wouldn't know that.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.240
Wait, was your last school
super good or something?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.450
Tch.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.200
So you're just uselessly big.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.200
Wha... Wh-What?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.790
What's his problem?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:03.660
Chika? Ah, Kimichika. Yeah, I remember him.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:09.540
Right? He must've been real
since you remember him, too.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.200
What? You thought he was a ghost?
Man, you're as stupid as ever.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:19.410
Do you know why he moved to Tokyo?

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:25.990
'Cause his mom died. I remember
the geezer going to her funeral.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:30.450
His pops was originally from Tokyo.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:34.160
I wonder why he came back here.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.040
Like I'd know. Ask him yourself.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.200
If I could, I wouldn't be in this mess.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.290
His barrier's impenetrable right now.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.620
Hey, do you think I'm uselessly big?

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.660
Didn't you know?

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:55.120
I'm someone you'd say is uselessly big.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.410
You ain't got nothin' on me. What?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.740
Is that really something to brag about?

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:00.330
Here.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.200
Yuni?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.700
Itoko Kuroba

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.830
Auntie says it's time for dinner.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.700
Hurry up and come home.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.590
Karaoke

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.620
How did Itoko know I was here?

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.290
Seriously, you're such an idiot.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.200
What...?

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.450
Kuroba.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:22.330
Chika... Haijima. What are
you doing out so late?

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.040
Club work.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.660
Club... You mean volleyball?

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.160
Today's practice, isn't it?

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.490
Yeah, but no one else was there, were they?

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.200
No.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.240
You were practicing by yourself?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.080
Yeah.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.790
Hey, you're Chika, aren't you?

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:42.790
Man, you really grew.
You're about as tall as Yuni.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.660
This is Yori. You remember him?

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:48.580
He's my cousin that came
to my gramps' place to play shogi.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:50.450
Yeah, I remember him.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.870
So what?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.700
Kuroba,

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.870
you sure are wasting your life.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.290
Wha--?

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:05.370
Wasting his life? And what?
You making good use of yours?

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:06.950
I am.

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:13.410
What's his problem? Man, he really
did change for the worse.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:16.660
He's like that at school, too, so he stands out.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:20.410
Dash.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:20.870
Right!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.330
Next.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.410
Right!

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.540
A spike serve... That's awesome.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.700
Hey, Transfer Student.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.370
You by yourself again?

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:09.200
As you can probably tell,
we don't have much room here.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.450
If you're gonna play by yourself,
couldn't you go off in the corner?

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.120
We could practice more efficiently
if we could use the full gym.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.450
I can't practice properly
unless I can use half the gym.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.490
It doesn't matter how many people you've got.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:25.490
If you don't have enough room to practice,
take it up with your advisor.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.240
What's your problem?
You just came to this school.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.790
Hey.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.450
You're not gonna complain
if he's not practicing by himself, right?

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:37.830
S-Sorry I'm late... Yeah.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.910
What's your deal?

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:42.450
I came to check you out.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.790
You had the nerve to say
that I was wastin' my life,

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:49.580
so I figured you must be doing
something really good with yours.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.830
Just so we're clear, I didn't
come to help you out.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:58.160
I just went with the flow earlier.
One against 20 isn't a fair fight.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:01.740
I'm not sure that two against 20
makes much of a difference.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:08.160
Man, you suck. That's exactly
why you don't have any friends.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:16.450
So, yeah. Those spike serves
earlier were pretty awesome.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:20.160
I need to get better, or I won't
be able to use them in matches.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.830
Ah, so that's why you kept doing serves?

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.410
That's about all I can do on my own.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.910
I don't have my tracksuit, but I guess
I wouldn't mind practicing with you.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:37.040
I don't have any plans with Yori today anyway.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:41.740
But I'm pretty sucky,
so I might not be much help.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:45.290
If you're better off on your own,
I won't come by anymore.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.910
What's your deal?

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.080
Hang on. I'm gonna go put my contacts in.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.790
Huh? Why?

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.740
I was holding back because
I was by myself anyway.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:12:00.160
Also, you suck at warming up.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.330
We're gonna start with
proper stretches. Just hang on.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:04.540
Huh?

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.950
"[Volleyball]"

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.950
"A sport where six players connect
with each other to ensure
the ball doesn't drop on their side."

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:17.290
Math, 95... Social studies, 99...

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.490
"Japanese"

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.920
Kimichika Haijima

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.160
So how the hell did you get a 30 in Japanese?

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.790
Shut up. How long are you
going to go on about this?

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.290
Ow...

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:30.080
Like you can talk. You got 42 in math,
and a 55 in social studies.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.700
If you're gonna talk about my scores,

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.870
how about mentioning the fact
that I got an 87 in Japanese?

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.240
Damn it, ow!

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.450
Man, this sucks.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.830
A warmup regimen from some famous
high school sure is something else.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.540
Kuroba, how tall are you right now?

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:48.620
Huh? I'm 173 centimeters.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.200
When did you last check?

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.490
Hm... Maybe fall?

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.200
175.0.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.330
Whoa, I grew two centimeters.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.620
Now measure me.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:08.540
172.7...

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:11.330
I grew, as well. You're
2 centimeters taller than me.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:15.040
2.3, actually. You're a setter, though.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.950
You don't have to worry
that much about height, do you?

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.330
There's a player that I like.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.910
Abe, who was chosen for the national team.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:25.450
They're a setter, but 191.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.450
The taller you are, the higher your sets are,

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.990
and you'll be more efficient
right up on the net.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.740
They're also ambidextrous and the dumps
they do with their left hand are amazing.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:38.240
Wait. You were using
both of your hands, too.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.580
I didn't know you were ambidextrous.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.410
I made myself ambidextrous.

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.290
You made yourself...?

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:44.830
Seriously?

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.490
What's up, Ryo?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:53.490
Hey, Yuni... I heard that the
volleyball team was practicing...

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:54.540
Oh, yeah. So--

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:55.910
Let's play.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:59.410
There're way more things
we can practice with three of us.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.740
1 month later

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.200
Hey, Kuroba.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.540
When we're doing practice games, you look at

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:01.790
the block before deciding on doing
a cross or a straight shot, aren't you?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.410
A cross or a straight?

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:07.040
Oh, the one where you hit
straight into the court is a straight,

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.040
and the one that's sorta hit
towards the outside is a cross.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.950
You've got it backwards, you fool.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.990
A spike that you hit diagonally
through the court is a cross.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.490
A hit that's parallel to the sideline
and goes straight through is a straight.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.580
When you're up front on the net,

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:22.910
you have a habit of stepping
while facing the middle,

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:25.200
so if you just naturally hit,
it'd be a cross shot,

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.540
and if you wanted to hit more
on the outside, it'd be a straight.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.290
That's really confusing.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:33.450
It's not, though. But whatever.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.370
I'll drill it into you.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.040
You'll what?

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.540
Even though you're not mentally getting it,

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.200
you've got good eyes,
so you're getting around the blocks.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:46.080
The way you use your upper body,
your flexible shoulders,

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.740
the way you can stay in the air...

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:51.870
Those are probably all talents
you naturally have.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.370
You'll get better...

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:58.580
...in no time if you actually put in
the work. You'll get taller, too.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.370
You feelin' okay?

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.700
What? Did I say something weird?

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.740
I mean... You always act like
you're better than everyone else

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:10.740
so I didn't think you'd actually
compliment or acknowledge anyone.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:14.950
Of course I'm going to acknowledge something
that deserves to be acknowledged.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:19.830
I mean... even if I'm good at volleyball,
it's not going to make me popular.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.370
Haijima, what are you going
to do about high school?

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:26.580
Are you going to go to school here?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.450
Yeah, that's what I'm planning to do, but...

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:32.620
But? There's a but to this?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:36.410
More importantly, there're gonna
be first-years joining in April.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:40.120
Yeah, you're right. You probably
shouldn't get your hopes up too much,

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.700
but we can probably snag one or two.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:45.080
If we get more members,
I want to enter a tournament.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:48.450
I don't know the schedule over here,

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.830
but before the national junior high tournament,

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:51.870
there should be a prefectural tournament.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:55.950
Even if we entered, I don't think
we'd actually be able to win.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.790
It's no fun if we don't do any matches.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:01.080
I want to do some matches.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.790
I'm going to make sure you're all
at least presentable by summer.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.580
I'll figure out the rest.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.410
Okay, fine.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.790
But we need an advisor
to enter a tournament, right?

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.200
Let's go ask around tomorrow.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:17.450
Hey. It's the rich boy
from the head family.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.410
Heya. It's been a while.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.040
Hey, Yori.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.580
I guess you guys are back in town.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.700
It's spring break for us college kids.

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.540
How much have you got on you today, rich boy?

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:32.490
Ah... I've only got some pocket change.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:35.490
I have to leave my bag lying
around more since I'm in a club.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:36.950
Club?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.700
I see. So that's what
Yorimichi was talking about.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.080
Volleyball, was it? Well, show us.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:47.870
Go on, show us a receive.
How did those look again?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.540
I totally forgot.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.200
Um... I think like this?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.160
Hey, looks like you got it down.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:57.490
You look cool, like you're
an actual volleyball player, rich boy.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:17:59.490
Haijima?

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:02.290
This isn't a game. Quit wasting
your time with them.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.370
Okay, you can stop pulling.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:06.870
But it is a game, isn't it, Yuni?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:13.410
Don't tell me you're actually serious
about this like that stupid jock there.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:16.540
Wait, are you mad about something, Yori?

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:19.290
I'm sorry we haven't been
hanging out much lately.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.870
Let's hang out during spring break.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.740
We have practice during spring break, too.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.540
But not every day, right?

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.910
If we're going to enter the summer tournament,

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.160
even that's not going to be enough.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.790
Seriously?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.660
Yuni...

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:37.240
You realize it, don't you?
You're not gonna make it.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:41.240
If you leave it as a game, you won't
make a fool outta yourself.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:46.160
I'm not very patient, so I ain't
gonna wait around for you that long.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:50.120
Hey, don't be so mean.
You're not serious, are you?

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.950
Man, you sure are popular, rich boy.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:57.120
Guess you're gonna have to end
a friendship with someone.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.580
Y-You understand, don't you?

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:05.160
We're cousins. I get really into things
but get bored just as quickly.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.580
I'm sure I'll get bored of volleyball soon...

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.410
Yeah.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.740
Are you being serious right now?

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:15.240
Er, I mean, uh...

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:16.830
Then quit right now.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.740
Things don't have to escalate that quickly.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.700
I don't want you ruining the tournament.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:22.990
Ruining...

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:25.080
I'm not letting this turn into a mess.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.120
I actually want to play some matches!

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.740
Looks like you've showed your true colors.

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:36.240
The genius setter from Meisei
with a shitty reputation

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:40.330
only cares about fulfilling
his own desires, huh?

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.330
Yori? What are you talking about?

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.540
You wanted to know yourself, Yuni.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.660
Why Chika came back here.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.200
Well, I looked it up for you.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.450
Hang on, now.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:56.540
You ain't gonna blame this on Yuni.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.990
You reap what you sow.

00:19:58.990 --> 00:19:59.830
Yori--

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.740
Out of the way, Yuni.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:08.330
I managed to get the school name easily
through your gramps since he knows ours.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:13.330
Then I looked it up online,
and man, did I hit the jackpot.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:18.790
Endless insults about the genius setter
that was at that school until last year.

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:21.740
Man, they really hate you.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.740
Yuni.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:25.910
Yeah?

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.620
It's not like I have a personal
vendetta against Chika.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.620
That doesn't matter anyway.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.580
This is all for your sake.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:37.620
Don't get too wrapped up in volleyball.

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.200
Why?

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:42.620
This guy will do whatever
it takes for volleyball.

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:45.290
And I mean anything.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.910
Play the damn game!

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.950
You're on the left, so your job
is to receive the ball!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:51.870
Then your job is to get
that ball to me, the setter!

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.660
How many times have I told you
just get the damn ball up?

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:58.330
If you can't even do that,
you don't deserve to spike the ball!

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.740
You won't be in the starting lineup
in tomorrow's game.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.330
I'm sure that'll make Yoshino and the others,

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:09.240
as well as the mothers calm down a bit.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:13.990
What? Hospital? Sota Yoshino's in the hospital?

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:16.950
They found him at home and he...

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:21.910
Listen up, Yuni. This jackass...

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:25.410
...pushed another teammate over
the edge for not listening to him,

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.620
and the kid tried to take his own life.
